# Solar collector control ACL template.
#
# This file is a reviewable template only. Provision usernames, passwords,
# certificates, and the final site list outside Git. Mosquitto denies topics
# for a principal when no matching read/write rule is granted.
#
# Keep the broker's password_file, this ACL, and TLS private key readable only
# by the Mosquitto service account and the designated operator account.

# Trusted management publisher: may issue commands and inspect safe state.
user solar-control
topic write solar/+/cmd/get-config
topic write solar/+/cmd/set
topic read solar/+/state/#

# Active collector: restrict command reads and data/state writes to configured
# sites. Add/remove explicit site blocks when the configured factory set
# changes; do not replace them with solar/# or solar/+/cmd/#.
user solar-collector
topic read solar/CL/cmd/#
topic write solar/CL/summary
topic write solar/CL/total_power_kw
topic write solar/CL/today_mwh
topic write solar/CL/month_mwh
topic write solar/CL/total_mwh
topic write solar/CL/zone/#
topic write solar/CL/status
topic write solar/CL/heartbeat
topic write solar/CL/alert
topic write solar/CL/state/#

topic read solar/KN/cmd/#
topic write solar/KN/summary
topic write solar/KN/total_power_kw
topic write solar/KN/today_mwh
topic write solar/KN/month_mwh
topic write solar/KN/total_mwh
topic write solar/KN/zone/#
topic write solar/KN/status
topic write solar/KN/heartbeat
topic write solar/KN/alert
topic write solar/KN/state/#

# Ordinary producer/observer: grant only the ordinary data/state reads or
# writes needed by the deployment. There is deliberately no cmd/# write rule.
user solar-observer
topic read solar/+/summary
topic read solar/+/total_power_kw
topic read solar/+/today_mwh
topic read solar/+/month_mwh
topic read solar/+/total_mwh
topic read solar/+/zone/#
topic read solar/+/status
topic read solar/+/heartbeat
topic read solar/+/alert
topic read solar/+/state/#

# Do not grant any principal write access to these legacy privileged paths:
#   solar/+/config
#   solar/+/set
# A temporary migration identity, if required by operations, must be narrowly
# scoped and removed before cutover; the collector never subscribes to them.
